{"name":"China Rose","hex":"#a8516e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"china","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of porcelain, a hard white translucent ceramic made from kaolin, now  sometimes distinguished in reference to tableware as fine or good china.","Chinaware: porcelain tableware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hibiscus × rosa-sinensis","blocks":[{"text":"Hibiscus × rosa-sinensis is a cultigen of tropical hibiscus, a flowering plant in the Hibiscus genus and Hibisceae tribe of the family Malvaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Hibiscus_Brilliant.jpg/330px-Hibiscus_Brilliant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus_%C3%97_rosa-sinensis"},{"title":"Rosa chinensis","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa chinensis, known commonly as the China rose, Chinese rose, or Bengal rose, is a member of the genus Rosa native to Southwest China in Guizhou, Hubei, and Sichuan Provinces. The first publication of Rosa chinensis was in 1768 by Nikolaus Joseph von Jacquin in Observationum Botanicarum, 3, p. 7 & plate 55."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Rosa_chinensis.jpg/330px-Rosa_chinensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_chinensis"},{"title":"China Rose (operetta)","blocks":[{"text":"China Rose is an operetta in two acts with music by A. Baldwin Sloane, and both lyrics and book by Harry L. Cort and George E. Stoddard. The work premiered in Boston at the Hollis Street Theatre on Christmas Eve of 1924. On December 30, 1924 portions of the work were performed by a live orchestra on WNAC radio in Boston."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Rose_(operetta)"},{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/White_coloured_flower_bud_of_Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis_at_night.jpg/500px-White_coloured_flower_bud_of_Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/White_coloured_flower_bud_of_Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis_at_night.jpg/960px-White_coloured_flower_bud_of_Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/White_coloured_flower_bud_of_Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis_at_night.jpg/500px-White_coloured_flower_bud_of_Hibiscus_rosa-sinensis_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t